[Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  all right hey everybody welcome back to  eight news now i'm monica jackson and it  is time for mondays with monica and  today we're talking about vaping i know  you guys have been seeing the  commercials  you've seen all the stories about it i  wonder if you know how very dangerous  this really is and it touched a  personal spot with me because i had a  grandmother who passed away as a result  of lung cancer  and as the vaccine rolls out kids may be  going back to school some might be doing  that hybrid thing so  i wanted to bring it back around because  it's very important dr jennifer pearson  is joining us this morning  thank you so much for being here uh dr  pearson tell us about  uh the nevada tobacco prevention  coalition and how you guys are tackling  all of this  yeah thank you for having me so the  nevada tobacco prevention coalition or  ntpc it's a collaborative effort between  organizations and individuals that work  in public health  in government medics medicine and  education  and our goal is to ultimately eliminate  the death and disease due to tobacco use  and second-hand smoke exposure in nevada  people think that this is a solved  problem but  we still have more than 400 000 people a  year in the united states dying from  tobacco use  it's primarily cigarette smoking but  we're starting to  see some concerning things happening  with vaping and e-cigarette use among  teens in 2019  high school students in nevada 22.5  percent of them reported vaping in the  last month  and that is very concerning even though  vaping is less harmful than smoking  cigarettes  and many adult smokers have found  e-cigarettes helpful in quitting smoking  saying something that's less harmful  than smoking is insane a lot because it  is by far the most harmful thing you can  do for your body  yeah and and here's what makes me mad dr  pearson  are there any laws in place any  legislation going through the pipeline  right now  to um get on top of these companies that  are peddling this stuff to kids  because it seems like somebody needs to  be held accountable  yeah absolutely i would say that the  main kind of action in that area  is that people are starting to sue  companies so you know companies often  say well that's not what we meant to do  right but and i can't speak to what they  meant to do because i can't read their  minds but  the reality is is that these companies  designed manufactured and marketed a  harmful  addictive product that nearly a quarter  of nevada's high school students have  used recently yeah and it is their  responsibility  to make sure that adolescents don't use  their products and so we're starting to  see people sue  companies like jewel it's a big one that  people hear about there's a  gigantic lawsuit of 786 people or  something like that happening right now  just starting to get going and i think  that's gonna we're gonna see some  some movement on that let's talk about  the top three things  the effects of this vaping because as i  was reading uh your information it was  just disgusting to me  what happens to a kid as they're  starting this horrible habit  give me the first one well sure  so you know vaping  nicotine among youth does open up a  bunch of concerns  so vaping  exposure during adolescence can affect  their brains it can affect how their  brains  are able to kind of process information  it can control how they can in the  future  um make uh decisions executive function  etc we're not a hundred percent sure on  the science on that quite yet but  even if it's biologically plausible and  therefore i think it's a  very good reason to avoid nicotine use  in adolescence  here's the one that really stuck with me  dr pearson it just grossed me out  chemical burns in the lungs of vapors  from nicotine and thc resemble the  damage  that was seen in the lungs of world war  one soldiers  who inhaled mustard gas are you kidding  me  well so that specific injury has been  linked to vaping  thc fluid so that's not linked to  to vaping nicotine fluid that's from  vaping  black market thc fluid that was cut with  uh vitamin e acetate yeah still however  baby nicotine does affect youths lungs  it causes  breathing problems i in my own research  i hear a lot about raising  excuse me wheezing and a hard time  breathing and coughing and the youth  that i talk to really  cite that they're having a hard time  performing and things like sports  they're having a hard time singing and  they are feeling like it wasn't worth it  for them to start it in the first place  a lot of them are dependent on nicotine  now they don't feel good  without vaping so that's why we have  these two different programs we have uh  behind the haze which is a commercial  and website that specifically speaks to  teens and then let's talk  vaping which is a website that is  trying to give tools to parents to talk  to their kids about vaping  absolutely let's talk vaping.com parents  check it out please  find out the details about this because  again as i was reading through it was  just disgusting to me  how these kids are taking up this  horrible habit and  as far as i'm concerned it's just as bad  as smoking i i've seen the effects of it  and it is not good  dr pearson thank you so much i  appreciate your time  thank you for having me absolutely all  right folks and don't forget join me on  the mlj show facebook live tonight  at 7 p.m where we'll have the recap of  the interview parents we got to get on  it because our kids are picking up some  bad habits

